don't preclude the use of Gnosis in the same turn.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd assume that Gurahl have the standard options when it comes to Rage use (suppression of wound penalties. extra actions, staying active and so on) with the ones listed on page 107 on top, but yes, this could certainly be written clearer, like many things in CB20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T08:46:47-07:00","id":605632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/605457-gurahl-extra-actions?p=605610#post605610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't consider that so clear-cut. Rage of the Mother Bear gives the option to transform Gnosis into multiple actions, at a ratio that would be ridiculous if it wasn't a rank 5 gift, particularly since these actions are made with a full dice pool and don't preclude the use of Gnosis in the same turn.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd assume that Gurahl have the standard options when it comes to Rage use (suppression of wound penalties. extra actions, staying active and so on) with the ones listed on page 107 on top, but yes, this could certainly be written clearer, like many things in CB20.</div> </div> 